les: 5/10 → 6/10 (+1 point)\n    50→- Overall: 7.70 → 7.85 (+0.15 point)\n    51→\n    52→## Current Issues (Priority Order)\n    53→\n    54→### HIGH\n    55→1. **Structured profile fields are empty (6/10)**\n    56→   - Problem: `appearance`, `personality`, `voice_guidance` are all null for both characters\n    57→   - The profile LLM is generating good content, but it's stored in `descriptions` array only\n    58→   - Impact: +0.15 points available if raised to 7/10 (would pass threshold)\n    59→   - Evidence: The descriptions text contains personality info like \"noble figure\", \"bold and aggressive\"\n    60→   - Root cause: `_generate_character_profile()` populates `descriptions` but not structured fields\n    61→   - Location: `src/analyzer.py` around line 1050-1100 (profile generation and population)\n    62→   - Fix: Extract structured data from LLM response OR modify LLM prompt to return structured fields\n    63→\n    64→### MEDIUM\n    65→2. **Canonical name format: \"the Prince Prospero\" should be \"Prince Prospero\"**\n    66→   - Problem: Leading article \"the\" shouldn't be part of a proper name\n    67→   - Impact: Minor usability issue\n    68→   - Location: Name normalization in character extraction\n    69→   - Fix: Strip leading \"the\" from proper noun canonical names\n    70→\n    71→3. **Missing alias \"the prince\" for Prospero**\n    72→   - Problem: Text uses \"the prince\" 6 times to refer to Prospero\n    73→   - Impact: Minor completeness issue\n    74→   - Location: Alias detection in character extraction\n    75→\n    76→4. **Pronunciation false positives (~35-40%)**\n    77→   - Problem: Common English words flagged: \"dauntless\", \"chiming\", \"magnificence\", \"buffoons\", etc.\n    78→   - Impact: +0.10 points available if reduced\n    79→   - 73 entries for a 2500-word text is excessive\n    80→   - Location: `src/agents/pronunciation.py` or pronunciation pipeline\n    81→   - Fix: Add frequency-based filtering to exclude common words\n    82→\n    83→### LOW\n    84→5. **Mention count doesn't include aliases**\n    85→   - Problem: \"the Prince Prospero\" shows 3 mentions, but \"Prospero\" appears 18 times\n    86→   - The combined count should be ~21\n    87→   - Location: Mention counting logic\n    88→\n    89→## Recommended Next Fix (Attempt 21)\n    90→\n    91→### Priority: Populate Structured Profile Fields (quickest path to 8.0)\n    92→\n    93→The profile generation is now running and producing good content in `descriptions`. The issue is that `appearance`, `personality`, and `voice_guidance` remain null.\n    94→\n    95→**Investigation needed:**\n    96→1. Check how `_generate_character_profile()` handles the LLM response\n    97→2. The LLM may be returning unstructured text that goes to `descriptions`\n    98→3. Need to either:\n    99→   a. Modify LLM prompt to return structured JSON with appearance/personality/voice_guidance\n   100→   b. Post-process the descriptions text to extract structured fields\n   101→   c. Modify the code that populates Character model to also set structured fields\n   102→\n   103→**Expected Impact:** +0.15+ points on Profiles (6→7), reaching 8.0 threshold\n   104→\n   105→## What NOT to Try Again\n   106→- Pre-merge substring matching (attempts 17-18) - FAILED\n   107→- Prompt-based rules (attempts 3, 14) - ineffective alone\n   108→- Context window adjustments (attempts 7-15) - insufficient\n   109→\n   110→## Fix History\n   111→\n   112→### Attempts 1-18\n   113→See git history and previous EVALUATION_STATE.md entries.\n   114→\n   115→### Attempt 19 - SUCCESS ✓\n   116→- **Change:** POST-PROCESSING cross-character alias fix\n   117→- **Files Modified:** `src/agents/characters.py` (added `_fix_misplaced_aliases()` method)\n   118→- **Result:** SUCCESS - Prospero alias correctly moved to Prince Prospero\n   119→- **Score Impact:** +1.0 overall (6.70 → 7.70)\n   120→- **Status:** Fix is working\n   121→\n   122→### Attempt 20 - PARTIAL SUCCESS\n   123→- **Change:** Adaptive MIN_MENTIONS_FOR_PROFILE threshold for short texts\n   124→- **Files Modified:** `src/analyzer.py` lines 1013-1025\n   125→- **Result:** PARTIAL - Profile stage runs (26.65s, 3 LLM calls, 2 items)\n   126→- **BUT:** Structured fields (appearance/personality/voice_guidance) still null\n   127→- **Score Impact:** +0.15 overall (7.70 → 7.85)\n   128→- **Status:** Profile generation works, but output format needs adjustment\n   129→\n   130→### Attempt 21 - IN PROGRESS\n   131→- **Change:** Populate structured profile fields (appearance, personality, voice_guidance)\n   132→- **Files Modified:** `src/analyzer.py` lines 1630-1806\n   133→- **Root Cause:** `_generate_character_profile()` was returning profile text which was stored in legacy `descriptions` field, but never populating the structured fields added in F8\n   134→- **Fix Details:**\n   135→  1. Modified LLM prompt to request structured JSON with appearance/personality/voice_guidance fields\n   136→  2. Updated return signature to include structured fields (now returns 6-tuple instead of 3-tuple)\n   137→  3. Updated calling code (line 1113) to unpack and store structured fields on character object\n   138→  4. Added fallback: if LLM doesn't return structured fields, use secondary LLM call to structure the profile text\n   139→- **Smoke Test:** Code runs without errors, all 444 unit tests pass\n   140→- **Status:** Ready for full evaluation\n   141→\n   142→## Next Action\n   143→**Phase:** awaiting_analysis\n   144→Re-run analysis on masque_of_red_death to verify structured profile fields are now populated.\n   145→\n   146→Expected score improvement: 6/10 → 7/10 on Character Profiles (+0.15 overall → 8.0 total)\n   147→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code,